      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with 0 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours and 11 cm over the last 7 days. Recent snowfall has left superb snow conditions, while overnight grooming means the morning will start firm and fast before softening into spring conditions through the day. Current conditions are 4°C, with 19 km/h winds and 32 km/h gusts. 9 of 10 lifts are open, including McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad; Wells Pipe Platter is closed. 10 of 10 terrain areas are open, including Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Big Willows, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit. The Main Basin and Valley View lifts were scheduled from 8:30am, with T-Bar, Captains, Soho and Willows following. Issued: 12:16 pm, 14 Sep. The access road is chain-free, but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle operating from the bottom of the access road. 4 of 5 car parks are open, with Car Park 1 full. The Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe and Gravity Cross parks are open; Olympic Pipe is closed and Big Air is on hold. A Schools Alpine Race is taking place on Upper Goldrush this morning from 8:45am. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 9 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
