      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with 0 cm of new snow overnight or in the last 24 hours and 17 cm over the last 7 days. Overnight grooming has produced classic spring skiing, with good snow coverage across the mountain. Current conditions are 5°C, with 14 km/h winds and 24 km/h gusts. A potential glide-slab issue may affect access to Saddle Basin, so skiers heading there are advised to go early; access may be closed if conditions deteriorate. All 3 lifts are open — Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter. 8 of 9 terrain areas are open, including Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Terrain Park; Motatapu Chutes is closed. All 11 listed groomed trails are open. Home Basin operates 8:30am–4:00pm and Saddle Basin 9:00am–3:30pm. Issued: 9:19 am, 14 Sep. The access road is chain-free, with chains to be carried and a free shuttle from the bottom of the access road. 4 of 5 car parks are open, with Car Park 1 full. The TC pop-up Terrain Park is operating by the old daylodge, and Te Wānanga o Aotearoa is holding a Māori Language Week kōrero on the Sun Deck at 12:30pm. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
